meta {
  name: 08 Create Invalid Patient
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/Patient
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/fhir+json
  Accept: application/fhir+json
}

body:json {
  {
    "resourceType": "Patient",
    "meta": { "tag": [ { "system": "urn:prohori", "code": "demo-cohort" } ] },
    "name": [ { "use": "official", "family": "Test", "given": ["Invalid"] } ],
    "gender": "banana",
    "birthDate": "1995-06-15"
  }
}

docs {
  # Force an error -> OperationOutcome

  - `gender` is bound to a **required** value set: `male | female | other | unknown`.
    `"banana"` is not in it.
  - Expect `400 Bad Request` (or `422`) with an `OperationOutcome`:
    - `issue[].severity` = `error`
    - `issue[].code` = `code-invalid` / `value`
    - `issue[].diagnostics` = human text pointing at `Patient.gender`
    - `issue[].expression` / `location` = the FHIRPath to the bad element
  - `OperationOutcome` is the standard error shape for EVERY failed FHIR
    interaction — your client parses this, not a bespoke error body.
}
